Design discussion: a local MCP server is needed to expose IntLoom to development tools. It should dispatch commands, initialize Runtime, load Workflows, and execute them. The proposed IntLoom CLI includes init to create a complete project directory at a selected path; the target layout and naming require later design. start checks whether the current directory is an IntLoom project and starts its local service, which initially also serves MCP. stop shuts down the service. flow executes a named Workflow with the user's intent. Review and improve this proposal, including command naming and the relationship between service startup and Workflow execution, and provide alternative approaches where useful.
